From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP kept SIM tickets stay entity-ticking after the cut

Packed fullcite splits onto a second thread, then west TNT fuse freezes.
The ticket wall zeros flood-propagated PLAYER sim through the hole, and
processLevelUpdates applied that 0 to kept chunks that still had their
own PLUGIN/FORCED tickets. Force-load was global-thread-only so region
prepare never planted FORCED. PLUGIN_TICKET lacked KEEP_DIMENSION_ACTIVE.
Do not clobber kept holders; allow force-load on the owning region;
plugin tickets keep a playerless shard ticking. Not bot herding, not
delete TNT. Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/scheduling/ChunkHolderManager.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/scheduling/ChunkHolderManager.java
@@ -483,11 +483,19 @@
                 final Long2ByteMap.Entry entry = iterator.next();
                 final long key = entry.getLongKey();
                 int newLevel = convertBetweenTicketLevels((int)entry.getByteValue());
+                final int cx = CoordinateUtils.getChunkX(key);
+                final int cz = CoordinateUtils.getChunkZ(key);
                 if (io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.YapRegionizerGap.blocksAddChunk(
-                        ChunkHolderManager.this.world,
-                        CoordinateUtils.getChunkX(key),
-                        CoordinateUtils.getChunkZ(key))) {
+                        ChunkHolderManager.this.world, cx, cz)) {
                     newLevel = MAX_TICKET_LEVEL + 1;
+                } else {
+                    // Cut-wall decrease can leave a kept chunk at BLOCK_TICKING (grass
+                    // still runs) while PLUGIN/FORCED tickets demand ENTITY_TICKING (TNT).
+                    final TicketSet kept = ChunkHolderManager.this.tickets.get(key);
+                    if (kept != null && !kept.isEmpty()) {
+                        final int ticketLevel = getTicketLevelAt(kept);
+                        if (ticketLevel < newLevel) {
+                            newLevel = ticketLevel;
+                        }
+                    }
                 }
 
                 NewChunkHolder current = ChunkHolderManager.this.chunkHolders.get(key);
